        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: French Montana, Machine Gun Kelly, MGK, Richard Colson Baker, Diddy, Nicki Minaj, Drake, Ace Hood, Lil Wayne, Birdman, The Weeknd, Rick Ross, 2 Chainz, Max B, Ne-Yo, Raekwon, Scarface, Snoop Dogg, Lee on the Beats, DJ Khaled, Bkorn\n- Products: Excuse My French, Pop That, Hold You Down\n- Places: Cleveland, Ohio\n- Topics: guest appearances, music production, mixtapes\n\nFacts:\n- In 2006, Machine Gun Kelly began his music career as a teenager by releasing a mixtape.\n- Richard Colson Baker, known as MGK or Machine Gun Kelly, was born on April 22, 1990, and he is an American rapper and actor from Cleveland, Ohio.\n- French Montana released “Pop That” as the first single from his 2013 debut studio album “Excuse My French.”\n- “Pop That” features guest appearances from Rick Ross, Drake, and Lil Wayne.\n- Lee on the Beats is best known for producing French Montana’s “Pop That” and for co-producing DJ Khaled’s “Hold You Down” with Bkorn.\n- French Montana’s album “Excuse My French” features guest appearances from Diddy, Nicki Minaj, Drake, Ace Hood, Lil Wayne, Birdman, The Weeknd, Rick Ross, 2 Chainz, Max B, Ne-Yo, Machine Gun Kelly, Raekwon, Scarface, and Snoop Dogg.",
